# EEG Attention Monitor — CNL Spec
# Demo 3: An SNN classifies attention state (focused vs. relaxed) from
# EEG alpha band power (8-12 Hz) using rate coding.
# High alpha → relaxed population fires; Low alpha → focused population fires.

The network MUST operate WITH timestep of 1 ms

The network MUST contain an excitatory sensory population of 1 neurons
The network MUST contain an inhibitory interneuron population of 35 neurons
The network MUST contain an excitatory motor population of 1 neurons

# Sensory population responds to alpha band power input
The sensory population MUST fire ONLY IF membrane potential exceeds 0.4

# Interneuron suppresses the output for relaxed alpha-dominant states
The interneuron population MUST fire ONLY IF membrane potential exceeds 0.5

# Motor population represents attention classification output
The motor population MUST emit a spike ONLY IF membrane potential exceeds 0.6

# Standard refractory periods
The sensory population MUST NOT fire DURING the refractory period of 0.002 seconds
The motor population MUST NOT fire DURING the refractory period of 0.002 seconds

# Slower time constants for EEG signal processing (alpha is 8-12 Hz)
The sensory population membrane potential MUST decay WITH time constant of 0.05 seconds
The motor population membrane potential MUST decay WITH time constant of 0.03 seconds

# Moderate coupling weight for rate-coded classification
The sensory population MUST project to motor population
The sensory population MUST project to interneuron population
The interneuron population MUST project to motor population

The connection from sensory population to motor population MUST have WITH synaptic weight of 1.0
The connection from sensory population to interneuron population MUST have WITH synaptic weight of 0.9
The connection from interneuron population to motor population MUST be inhibitory with weight of -0.6

# Transmission delay reflecting thalamocortical pathway
A synapse MUST have a transmission delay of 10ms
